sys_script.script:
/**
 * SUPPRESSED -- the body below is intentionally commented out. The business rule record is kept
 * so the suppression is visible in the update set and reversible without recreating it.
 *
 * Why: conflict detection moved into the discovery pipeline. IllumioDiscoveryUtils.evaluateConflict
 * decides `conflicts` from the CMDB and PCE values already in memory while the workload is being
 * processed, and writes it as part of the same insert/update. This rule then ran afterwards and
 * re-decided the same field -- one re-read of the PCE configuration and its label dimension
 * mappings per workload row, on the hottest write path in the app, to arrive at an answer that
 * had just been computed. On a 5k+ run that is 5k+ redundant configuration reads.
 *
 * It was also not merely redundant. Running after the fact, it could overwrite a `conflicts` value
 * that evaluateConflict had deliberately set to false.
 *
 * If conflict detection ever needs to move back out of discovery, restore this rule and remove the
 * evaluateConflict call rather than running both.
 */

